{"raw": {"https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-master-of-occupational-therapy-program/": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Master of Occupational Therapy Program - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Master of Occupational Therapy Program Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Master of Occupational Therapy Program Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Master of Occupational Therapy Program School of Nursing and Health Professions Salary: $990/per Credit Trinity Washington University invites applications for Adjunct Faculty in the Maser of Occupational Therapy Program within the School of Nursing and Health Professions for Spring 2027. The program is seeking applicants who possess clinical expertise and teaching experience in at least one of the following areas: Psychosocial and behavioral health assessment and intervention Functional cognition assessment and intervention Research Knowledge and experience in distance/online education is recommended but not required. QUALIFICATIONS: Successful candidates must have the following credentials: Master\u2019s degree in occupational therapy or related field District of Columbia licensure as an Occupational Therapist (or eligibility) At least one year experience as an Occupational Therapist Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to Adjunct Professors to include, Supplemental Personal Insurance (AFLAC), 403(b) Retirement Plan \u2013 Group Supplemental Retirement Account (GSRA), Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and dining services. Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Menu"}, "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-occupational-therapy-assistant-program/": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Occupational Therapy Assistant Program", "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Occupational Therapy Assistant Program - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Occupational Therapy Assistant Program Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Adjunct Faculty \u2013 Occupational Therapy Assistant Program Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Salary: $990/per Credit Trinity Washington University invites applications for an instructor in the baccalaureate occupational therapy assistant program within the School of Nursing and Health Professions for Spring 2027. The program is seeking applicants who possess teaching experience and/or clinical expertise in at least one of the following areas: Pediatrics intervention Mental/behavioral health intervention Adult physical disability intervention In collaboration with the program director, the candidate will be involved in curriculum design, strategic planning, teaching, and student advising. QUALIFICATIONS: Successful candidates must have the following credentials: Certified Occupational Therapy Assistant (NBCOT) Minimum of one-year clinical experience as a COTA Washington, DC OTA License or eligibility for licensure Baccalaureate Degree Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to Adjunct Professors to include, Supplemental Personal Insurance (AFLAC), 403(b) Retirement Plan \u2013 Group Supplemental Retirement Account (GSRA), Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and dining services Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"}, "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/assistant-basketball-coach-3/": {"title": "Assistant Basketball Coach", "description": "Assistant Basketball Coach - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Assistant Basketball Coach Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Assistant Basketball Coach Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Assistant Basketball Coach Salary 3k Trinity Washington University seeks a dynamic part-time Assistant Basketball Coach for the women\u2019s basketball team. Trinity Washington is part of the USCAA (United States Collegiate Athletic Association). Founded in 1897 as one of the nation\u2019s historic Catholic women\u2019s colleges, Trinity today continues as both a Predominantly Black and Hispanic Serving institution. As a mission-driven university devoted to providing access and educational excellence to underserved populations of students, Trinity welcomes professionals with demonstrated interest and experience in working with diverse cultural populations including black, Hispanic multi-cultural and non-traditional college and graduate students. Responsibilities: Support the mission and vision of Trinity Washington University and the Athletics department. Ability to comply with all department rules, regulations and protocols. Assist head coach with all aspects of the basketball program. Prior player experience preferred. Conduct player evaluations at the beginning of the season, coach players of all skill levels. Help design practice plans, lead skill-development drills, and teach sport-specific tactics on the floor. Foster team bonding and team morale. Assist with team practices and conditioning sessions. Serve as a mentor to athletes, helping resolve academic and non-academic issues. Provide support and encouraging feedback to team. Monitor academic performance and general behavior of student athletes. Recruit and coach student athletes regularly and ensure that all student athletes take part in practice sessions regularly. Assist with team travel logistics, equipment inventory, and summer camps or clinics. Qualifications: Must have demonstrated success in coaching basketball at the collegiate or high school level, and/or as a basketball player at the college level. Bachelor\u2019s degree and previous recruiting experience is preferred. Thorough understanding of game rules and coaching techniques. Leadership and communication skills. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to part-time employees to include, Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account, Transit Expense Account, Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Supplemental Personal Insurance (Aflac), 403(b) Retirement Plan, General Leave, Paid Holidays, Trinity Center Membership, On-Campus Parking, Shuttle Bus Service and Dining Services. Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"}, "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-financial-aid/": {"title": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid", "description": "Assistant Director of Financial Aid - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Assistant Director of Financial Aid Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Assistant Director of Financial Aid Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Assistant Director of Financial Aid Salary Range: 65k to 70k ( Salary determination is based on experience & qualifications Trinity Washington University seeks an Assistant Director of Financial Aid located in Enrollment Services. The Assistant Director of Financial Aid is responsible for managing financial aid, billing, educational financing and related services for Trinity students. In this position you will have a vital role in the management of the Federal financial programs, as well as some operations of PowerFAIDS, which is the student financial aid management system used by Trinity. The primary goal in this role is to provide comprehensive financial aid guidance, support and resources to help students achieve their educational goals at Trinity Washington University. This position will report directly to the Vice President for Enrollment Services. Education Requirements & Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s Degree in appropriate field such as business, finance, education or public administration. 3 to 5 years of hands-on experience in a post-secondary financial aid office. Deep understanding of federal Title IV regulations, state programs, and institutional compliance standards. Proficiency with financial aid software and data systems such as PowerFAIDS. Responsibilities & Functions: Administer, maintain and reconcile the Federal Direct Student Loan Program and Federal Pell Grant programs. Stay current on all federal, state, and institutional regulations and policies. Serve as liaison with Technology Services, College Board, COD, NSLDS, and other partners in electronic data exchange. Oversee all external updates to PowerFAIDS. Responsible for transmitting and receiving all electronic data from PowerFAIDS to the U.S. Department of Education. Complete monthly reconciliation for Federal Direct Loans and Pell programs. Assist in the preparation of various office reports (e.g. FISAP, end-of-year, etc.) all related to financial aid programs. Download loan counseling and MPN data. Process all loan certifications and submit all disbursement rosters for processing. Manage and send financial aid information, requests and updates to students through PowerFAIDS. Create workflow processes to improve efficiency. Monitor and resolve data integration errors and COD errors. Download and screen all incoming ISIRs, verify selected ISIRs, resolve rejects as required. Participate in professional training workshops as required. Provide accurate and timely assistance to students, parents, faculty and staff regarding enrollment and financial aid. Work closely with other administrative offices to assist in the recruitment and retention of students. Assist with Open House, New Student Orientation, and other special campus events, as needed. Comply with confidentiality requirements as set by HIPAA, FERPA, federal, and state and local regulation. Other duties as requested by the Vice President for Enrollment Services. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong verbal and written skills to guide students and families through financial processes. Ability to manage heavy workloads, meet funding deadlines, and solve problems. Demonstrated ability to work in a team, support diverse populations, and assistant with daily administrative oversight. Working knowledge of Title IV regulations. Strong proficiency in Aid Management Software. Strong customer service and interpersonal communication skills. Familiarity with federal grants, direct loans, work-study administration, and institutional or state scholarship criteria. Strong knowledge of federal platforms. Hands-on experience with financial aid software systems such as PowerFAID. Ability to run reports, complete reconciliation processes, and utilize data to support administrative decisions. Demonstrated ability to problem-solve, and use high degree of professional judgement. Excellent time management skills in prioritizing tasks and managing multiple shifting deadlines in a high-volume, fast-paced environment. Ability to work cross-functionally in a collaborative environment with Admissions, the Registrar, etc. to support student recruitment and retention goals. High degree of discretion for handling sensitive and confidential financial records with empathy and integrity. Strong working knowledge of Microsoft office. Schedule and Work Environment: 40 hours per week minimum, including regular office hours to support the business hours of the University: 9am to 7pm. Includes regular Saturday hours 8am to 2pm. This is an all year-around, 12-month, full-time, in-person position. Ability to work efficiently with many interruptions from walk-ins, telephone inquiries and other student requests. The noise level is usually quiet. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to full-time employees to include Health, Dental & Vision insurance, Employer Paid Life and Disability benefits, 403(b) Retirement plan with employer match up to 6%, Paid Family Leave, Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and more. Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"}, "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/assistant-soccer-coach-3/": {"title": "Assistant Soccer Coach", "description": "Assistant Soccer Coach - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Assistant Soccer Coach Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Assistant Soccer Coach Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Assistant Soccer Coach 3k (Seasonal) \u2013 Season currently in session \u2013 salary amount will be pro-rated. Trinity Washington University seeks a dynamic part-time Assistant Soccer Coach for the women\u2019s soccer team.\u00a0Trinity is part of the USCAA (United States Collegiate Athletic Association). Founded in 1897 as one of the nation\u2019s historic Catholic women\u2019s colleges, Trinity today continues as both a Predominantly Black and Hispanic Serving institution. As a mission-driven university devoted to providing access and educational excellence to underserved populations of students, Trinity welcomes professionals with demonstrated interest and experience in working with diverse cultural populations including black, Hispanic multi-cultural and non-traditional college and graduate students. Position Responsibilities: Support the mission and vision of Trinity Washington University and the Athletics department. Comply with all department rules, regulations, and protocols. Assist the head coach with all aspects of the soccer program. Prior player experience preferred. Conduct player evaluations at the beginning of the season, coach players of all skill levels. Foster team bonding and team morale. Assist with team practices and conditioning sessions. Assist in designing and executing daily training sessions. Assist with team travel logistics (meals, lodging, transport), equipment inventory,etc. Serve as mentor to athletes, helping resolve academic and non-academic issues. Provide support and efficient feedback to the team. Monitor academic performance and general behavior of student-athletes. Recruit and coach student-athletes regularly and ensure that all student-athletes take part in practice sessions regularly. Qualifications: Must have demonstrated success in coaching soccer at the collegiate or high school level, and/or as a soccer player at the college level. Bachelor\u2019s degree and previous recruiting experience are preferred. Thorough understanding of game rules and coaching techniques. Leadership and communication skills. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to part-time employees to include, Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account, Transit Expense Account, Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Supplemental Personal Insurance (Aflac), 403(b) Retirement Plan, General Leave, Paid Holidays, Trinity Center Membership, On-Campus Parking, Shuttle Bus Service and Dining Services. Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"}, "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/assistant-volleyball-coach-3/": {"title": "Assistant Volleyball Coach", "description": "Assistant Volleyball Coach - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Assistant Volleyball Coach Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Assistant Volleyball Coach Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Assistant Volleyball Coach 3k (Seasonal) \u2013 Season currently in session \u2013 salary amount will be pro-rated. Trinity Washington University seeks a dynamic part-time Assistant Volleyball Coach for the women\u2019s soccer team.\u00a0USCAA (United States Collegiate Athletic Association). Founded in 1897 as one of the nation\u2019s historic Catholic women\u2019s colleges, Trinity today continues as both a Predominantly Black and Hispanic Serving institution. As a mission-driven university devoted to providing access and educational excellence to underserved populations of students, Trinity welcomes professionals with demonstrated interest and experience in working with diverse cultural populations including black, Hispanic multi-cultural and non-traditional college and graduate students. Position Responsibilities: Support the mission and vision of Trinity Washington University and the Athletics department. Comply with all department rules, regulations, and protocols. Assist the head coach with all aspects of the soccer program. Prior player experience preferred. Assist with planning and executing daily practices. Lead technical training (e.g., passing, setting, attacking, blocking) and implement team defensive/offensive systems. Conduct player evaluations at the beginning of the season, coach players of all skill levels. Foster team bonding and team morale. Assist with team practices and conditioning sessions. Serve as mentor to athletes, helping resolve academic and non-academic issues. Provide support and efficient feedback to the team. Monitor academic performance and general behavior of student-athletes. Recruit and coach student-athletes regularly and ensure that all student-athletes take part in practice sessions regularly. Qualifications: Must have demonstrated success in coaching volleyball at the collegiate or high school level, and/or as a volleyball player at the college level. Bachelor\u2019s degree and previous recruiting experience are preferred. Thorough understanding of game rules and coaching techniques. Leadership and communication skills. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to part-time employees to include, Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account, Transit Expense Account, Employee Assistance Program (EAP), Supplemental Personal Insurance (Aflac), 403(b) Retirement Plan, General Leave, Paid Holidays, Trinity Center Membership, On-Campus Parking, Shuttle Bus Service and Dining Services. Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"}, "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/dean-of-the-school-of-nursing-and-health-professions/": {"title": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions", "description": "Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Professions Salary Range: $160,000 to $180,000 Trinity in Washington, a comprehensive university in the nation\u2019s capital, seeks a Dean for the School of Nursing and Health Professions (NHP).\u00a0 The Dean is the chief academic and administrative leader for the school, providing strategic vision, academic oversight, and operational management for a diverse portfolio of undergraduate and graduate programs.\u00a0 Enrolling about 300 students, NHP includes undergraduate programs in Nursing, Occupational Therapy, Public Health, and Social Work, as well as graduate programs in Counseling, Occupational Therapy, and Public Health. The Dean is responsible for fostering academic excellence, supporting faculty and student success, strengthening external partnerships, and advancing the Trinity\u2019s commitment to social justice, health equity, and community engagement. Reporting to the Provost and supervising a staff including 19 full-time faculty and 13 administrative staff as well as adjunct faculty as needed, the Dean is responsible to oversee the design and development of academic programs, ensuring that all programs meet accreditation and regulatory standards including CCNE, ACOTE, CACREP, CSWE and the D.C. Board of Nursing.\u00a0 The Dean leads faculty hiring and assessment along with faculty professional development.\u00a0 The Dean is responsible to manage the unit budget and to steward significant gifts and grants supporting the unit\u2019s programs and students.\u00a0 With the faculty, the Dean also builds and sustains strong partnership relationships for clinical placements and career pathways with healthcare systems, clinical agencies, community organizations and governmental partners throughout the Washington region. Candidates must present an earned doctorate in a field in which Trinity has a program including nursing, public health, counseling, occupational therapy, social work, or closely related health professions fields.\u00a0 Candidates should also present an academic track record that includes (a) experience as a faculty member in a related academic program, and (b) at least 3 years of successful experience as a dean or equivalent senior academic administrator, and (c) scholarly and professional achievements supporting appointment at the most senior level.\u00a0 Experience with interprofessional healthcare education is a plus.\u00a0 Along with the academic credentials, candidates should also present at least three years of clinical experience in one of the major fields in Trinity\u2019s curriculum.\u00a0 Experience with the healthcare systems in the Washington region is an advantage.\u00a0\u00a0 Candidates must also have demonstrated success managing a diverse workforce to satisfy professional expectations and to achieve goals across all programs. Trinity Washington University is one of the nation\u2019s historic Catholic women\u2019s colleges, sustaining a commitment to women\u2019s education in the daytime liberal arts programs while also offering coeducational professional and graduate programs including those in NHP.\u00a0 Trinity enrolls about 2,000 students and is classified as a Predominantly Black/Hispanic Serving institution.\u00a0 About half of Trinity\u2019s students are D.C. residents; about 60% of undergraduates are Pell grantees. Position starts January 1, 2027. Candidates with the specified credentials should submit a complete c.v. along with a cover letter when applying with no more than two pages specifying alignment with these position requirements. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to full-time employees to include Health, Dental & Vision insurance, Employer Paid Life and Disability benefits, 403(b) Retirement plan with employer match up to 6%, Paid Family Leave, Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and more. Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Menu"}, "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/director-of-annual-giving/": {"title": "Director of Annual Giving", "description": "Director of Annual Giving - Trinity Washington University | Washington, DC Skip to main content TRINITY WASHINGTON UNIVERSITY Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity Close Search search Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus search Director of Annual Giving Home \u00bb Jobs \u00bb Director of Annual Giving Menu HR Home Employment Opportunities Employee Resources Student Employment Trinity Institute Director of Annual Giving Salary Range: 95k to 105k ( Salary determination is based on experience & qualifications) Trinity Washington University seeks a Director of Annual Giving. The Director of Annual Giving secures current use unrestricted support for the university from alumnae and alumni, parents and family, and friends of Trinity Washington University. Position Summary The Director plans, manages and will focus on building a year-round fundraising plan for the Annual Fund, the foundation of Trinity\u2019s fundraising initiatives.\u00a0 The fundraising plan will include goals, strategies, and programming that aim to build and engage our donor base through a variety of means including direct mail, online giving, email, crowdfunding, personal phone outreach, and events. This person will also work to ensure effective administration of annual fund gifts through acknowledgment letters, recognition of donors, and the delivery of any necessary reports and communications, such as pledge reminders, to appropriate constituents. This position reports to the Director of Development and Alumnae/i Relations. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Work collaboratively with Director of Development to create and manage a comprehensive fundraising plan and appeal schedule for the Annual Fund: Set dollar, participation, and qualitative goals for the annual giving program. Create and implement strategies to achieve Annual Fund goals. Create and manage a calendar/schedule of multidimensional appeals that leverages a variety of media (email solicitation, direct mail appeals, face-to-face solicitations, events) to communicate with potential and current donors. Assess program at the end of the year and lead annual planning process. Build relationships with constituents and personally solicit an assigned pool of prospects as appropriate. Utilize Raiser\u2019s Edge to track visits, produce contact notes, and conduct appropriate constituent follow-up. Draft and coordinate Annual Fund and solicitation and acknowledgement letters. Analyze results of the fund and reunion campaign by tracking progress from year to year and generate reports for review. Contribute content to university publications and social media as appropriate. Attend on-campus and off-campus events, as appropriate. Assist with prospect research. Other responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Development. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree or equivalent. At least five years of relevant experience in a development-related role in an educational environment, ideally in higher education. Strong knowledge of Raiser\u2019s Edge software. Proven track record managing an annual campaign. Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to communicate clearly and effectively, verbally and in writing. Positive attitude, flexible approach, and ability to collaborate. Trinity offers comprehensive and competitive benefits to full-time employees to include Health, Dental & Vision insurance, Employer Paid Life and Disability benefits, 403(b) Retirement plan with employer match up to 6%, Paid Family Leave, Trinity Center Membership Free to all employees to include full size pool, walking track, weight & Cardio equipment, Free campus parking, Free Shuttle bus between campus & Brookland Metro station and more. Qualified, interested applicants, please\u2026 Apply Now Trinity Washington University is dedicated to the achievement of excellence and diversity among its students, faculty, and staff. Trinity is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive community and strongly encourages all qualified individuals to apply. \u00a9 2026 Trinity Washington University 125 Michigan Ave. NE Washington, DC 20017 202-884-9000 Close Menu Academics Academic Programs All Academic Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Continuing Education Schools College of Arts & Sciences School of Nursing & Health Professions School of Professional & Graduate Studies School of Education Academic Resources Academic Support Services Library Bookstore Catalog Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Get Started Request Information Apply Now Tours and Events Admissions Office Special Groups Transfer Students Undocumented Students Military & Veterans International Students Affording Your Education How Trinity Lowers Your Costs Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Student Experience Campus Life Student Affairs Campus Housing Dining Services Gym & Athletic Center Student Support Center for Student Success Academic Support Services Library Services Career Services Activities Trinity Times Athletics Clubs & Organizations Student Government About About Trinity Mission & History President & Board Accreditation Right-to-Know Info Policies & Handbooks Website A-Z People & Offices Who\u2019s Who at Trinity Directory Offices Work at Trinity Visit & Events All Campus Calendar Host Your Event at Trinity Visiting Campus Request Info Alumnae/i Donate My Trinity"}}, "rows": {"https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-master-of-occupational-therapy-program/": {"school_id": 209, "posting_url": "https://www2.trinitydc.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-master-of-occupational-therapy-program/", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Faculty", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadli